WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.666 --> 00:00:14.687
rainy season arrived.

2
00:00:15.447 --> 00:00:17.008
But this time it seemed to pass quickly.

3
00:00:17.749 --> 00:00:19.890
That was because we now had Jenny with us.

4
00:00:20.771 --> 00:00:23.513
Her lively spirits and good conversation kept us happy.

5
00:00:24.394 --> 00:00:28.656
She and the boys told many wondrous tales to entertain everyone during the evenings.

6
00:00:29.637 --> 00:00:33.540
At last the rains ceased, and we stepped out into the spring air.

7
00:00:34.712 --> 00:00:38.394
After the rainy season, our various properties required attention.

8
00:00:39.294 --> 00:00:42.555
Jack and Franz spent a day working on the island in the bay.

9
00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:46.717
They repaired the watchtower and put the two cannons in working order.

10
00:00:47.498 --> 00:00:50.559
As evening drew near, the rest of us strolled along the beach.

11
00:00:51.459 --> 00:00:54.200
We watched Jack and Franz as they completed their work.

12
00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:56.822
Soon it was time for target practice.

13
00:00:57.662 --> 00:01:02.324
Paddling off in the kayak, Jack and Franz left an empty tub at a distance from the island.

14
00:01:03.116 --> 00:01:04.697
They returned to the island and fired.

15
00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:09.220
The tub shattered into pieces, and the boys shouted with triumph.

16
00:01:10.161 --> 00:01:14.144
As their shouts died away, we heard three cannons booming in response.

17
00:01:14.164 --> 00:01:16.686
"Could that possibly be from a ship?"

18
00:01:17.126 --> 00:01:17.646
asked Fritz.

19
00:01:17.666 --> 00:01:20.849
"It sounded like it came from the west," said Ernest.

20
00:01:20.869 --> 00:01:25.092
"Maybe it was just the boys firing again," suggested Jenny.

21
00:01:25.772 --> 00:01:28.674
But Jack and Franz were paddling as fast as they could toward us.

22
00:01:29.535 --> 00:01:30.836
They must have heard the sound too.

23
00:01:31.804 --> 00:01:33.585
So many questions rushed through my mind.

24
00:01:34.385 --> 00:01:36.085
Was a European ship nearby?

25
00:01:36.525 --> 00:01:37.866
Or was it a Malay pirate?

26
00:01:38.586 --> 00:01:40.806
What would happen when we met our fellow humans?

27
00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:43.107
Would they be friends who would help us?

28
00:01:43.567 --> 00:01:45.328
Would they be enemies who would attack us?

29
00:01:46.288 --> 00:01:49.249
Or would they be poor, unfortunate creatures who needed our help?

30
00:01:49.989 --> 00:01:53.130
Before I could say anything, Jack and Franz were onshore.

31
00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:54.770
"Did you hear them?"

32
00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:55.811
gasped Jack.

33
00:01:55.831 --> 00:01:57.251
"What shall we do?

34
00:01:57.611 --> 00:01:58.331
Where shall we go?"

35
00:01:58.351 --> 00:01:59.912
"Oh, Fritz!"

36
00:02:00.272 --> 00:02:03.049
said Franz, grasping his oldest brother's hands.

37
00:02:03.849 --> 00:02:05.589
"It must be a European ship.

38
00:02:06.329 --> 00:02:07.290
We shall find it.

39
00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:10.450
We shall see Switzerland once more!"

40
00:02:11.371 --> 00:02:15.052
Until then I did not realize how much the two boys longed to return to Europe.

41
00:02:15.972 --> 00:02:16.632
"What should we do?"

42
00:02:16.992 --> 00:02:17.572
asked Fritz.

43
00:02:18.453 --> 00:02:20.373
"We can't do anything right now," I said.

44
00:02:20.393 --> 00:02:22.134
"It is growing dark.

45
00:02:22.694 --> 00:02:24.234
We will have to wait until tomorrow."

46
00:02:25.074 --> 00:02:27.135
We returned to Rockburg in the greatest excitement.

47
00:02:27.875 --> 00:02:30.916
Everyone was talking eagerly, and no one went to bed until late.

48
00:02:31.656 --> 00:02:35.778
That night the boys and I took turns keeping watch in case more signals were fired.

49
00:02:36.559 --> 00:02:38.860
In the middle of the night, the wind began to blow.

50
00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:44.043
And for the next two days, a fearful storm kept us impatiently trapped at home.

51
00:02:44.983 --> 00:02:49.586
On the third morning the skies cleared, and I set off to the island with Jack and Franz.

52
00:02:50.466 --> 00:02:52.707
I was worried that the storm had destroyed the ship.

53
00:02:53.368 --> 00:02:56.930
Or that it had gone out to sea to weather the storm and would not return.

54
00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:58.711
We fired the cannons.

55
00:02:59.831 --> 00:03:00.972
One. Two.

56
00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:02.620
And then we waited.

57
00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:05.201
For some minutes there was no reply.

58
00:03:06.001 --> 00:03:08.682
Then we heard the answering sound of cannons in the distance.

59
00:03:08.702 --> 00:03:10.482
"They're still nearby!"

60
00:03:10.822 --> 00:03:11.443
shouted Jack.

61
00:03:12.183 --> 00:03:16.224
We quickly returned to shore, where the family was in the greatest state of excitement.

62
00:03:17.104 --> 00:03:17.884
"Calm yourselves!"

63
00:03:18.225 --> 00:03:18.965
I said to everyone.

64
00:03:18.985 --> 00:03:21.845
"I don't know the answers yet to any of your questions."

65
00:03:22.806 --> 00:03:24.346
Fritz and I prepared to investigate.

66
00:03:25.086 --> 00:03:28.927
Well-armed and equipped with a telescope, we seated ourselves in the kayak.

67
00:03:29.688 --> 00:03:30.728
"Be careful!"

68
00:03:31.072 --> 00:03:32.593
called my wife as we set off.

69
00:03:33.573 --> 00:03:36.614
We paddled out of the bay and around the high cliffs to our left.

70
00:03:37.495 --> 00:03:41.596
For almost an hour we proceeded in the direction from which the cannon sounds had come.

71
00:03:42.497 --> 00:03:45.138
But we saw nothing until we came to a small cove.

72
00:03:46.038 --> 00:03:47.899
Then suddenly we saw a large ship!

73
00:03:48.619 --> 00:03:52.161
Keeping our kayak close to the cliff, I peered through the telescope.

74
00:03:52.921 --> 00:03:54.922
I did not want those on board to see us.

75
00:03:54.942 --> 00:04:01.124
"It's an English naval ship," I said, "and there are some tents pitched onshore."

76
00:04:01.144 --> 00:04:02.445
I handed the telescope to Fritz.

77
00:04:03.346 --> 00:04:04.927
But I began to have some concerns.

78
00:04:04.947 --> 00:04:06.628
"Why is this ship here?"

79
00:04:07.088 --> 00:04:07.508
I asked.

80
00:04:07.528 --> 00:04:10.671
"It's so far off the usual shipping routes.

81
00:04:11.571 --> 00:04:14.913
Perhaps its crew has done away with the captain and seized the ship?"

82
00:04:15.874 --> 00:04:16.434
"No, Father!"

83
00:04:16.715 --> 00:04:17.395
Fritz exclaimed.

84
00:04:17.415 --> 00:04:20.077
"I can see the captain talking to one of the officers.

85
00:04:20.877 --> 00:04:21.918
All looks well on board.

86
00:04:22.238 --> 00:04:23.559
Take another look."

87
00:04:23.579 --> 00:04:26.541
He handed the telescope back to me, and I saw that he was right.

88
00:04:26.561 --> 00:04:28.522
"Let's go to them at once!"

89
00:04:28.923 --> 00:04:30.704
said Fritz, taking up his paddle.

90
00:04:31.432 --> 00:04:32.614
"No," I said firmly.

91
00:04:32.634 --> 00:04:36.079
"I do not want to appear before these strangers like this.

92
00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:39.143
We will go home and gather up the whole family.

93
00:04:39.864 --> 00:04:44.751
Dressed in our finest clothing, we will return in the sailboat and welcome these men to our shores."
